<Page title="Colophon" description="How this site is made, and why it looks the way it does.">
	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and published from a public
			GitHub repository via GitHub Pages. No trackers, no cookies, no popups.
		</p>
		<p>
			The type is <a href="https://www.brailleinstitute.org/freefont/">Atkinson Hyperlegible</a>,
			designed by the Braille Institute for maximum legibility — a font built on the belief that
			reading should be easy for everyone, which is also what the writing here aims for.
		</p>
		<p>
			The accent color is Falu red — the traditional Swedish barn paint that happens to also be
			the red of New England barns. Two high-latitude, forested, maritime places; one pigment.
			That coincidence is roughly the thesis of this site.
		</p>
		<p>
			The design intends to be calm and a little imperfect: no shadows, almost no motion, revision
			dates shown honestly, and open questions published before they're answered. If a page feels
			unfinished, that's because it is. <em>This is a working table, and tables stay in use.</em>
		</p>
	</div>
</Page>
